# Test: a link-local single-hop BFD peer that names no interface is refused.
#
# VALIDATES: `ze config validate` refuses `single-hop-session fe80::b` with no
#            `interface`, naming the peer and saying to add `interface` (AC-5 of
#            spec-bfd-link-local-peer-zone). The bfd plugin's verify runs
#            parseSingleHopSession over the committed tree.
# PREVENTS: a link-local session loading with no link and sending on whichever
#           link the kernel's fe80::/64 route lookup picks (RFC 5881 Section 3).

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bfd {
    enabled true;
    bind-v6 true;
    single-hop-session fe80::b {
        local fe80::a;
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=bfd: single-hop-session fe80::b: a link-local peer is on one link only: add interface naming the link it is on
